{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>ואף</b> [and moreover] lacks [the word] איש, as in: ואני תפלה אל תהי מרי (1 Samuel 1:16)." "A man of wine — he is treacherous, arrogant, committing outrage." "<b>ולא ינוה</b> — he will not rest in a dwelling, for his entire desire is to go about destroying." "<b>ויאסף אליו</b> — as death does, so that no man escapes his hand."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:09.507486985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}